# B
Yes, proceed, but split the work into **two tracks**.

The current corrected pooled P3a track should finish its saved-artifact diagnostics. Do not interrupt it. But the couples-draw issue is important enough that it should become the **main next-specification-cycle design problem**, alongside occupation-conditional wages.

The key point is that the couples issue is not just “we need more draws.” Your note correctly states that the current couples construction is a **diagonal** of the male × female opportunity space: his draw (i) is paired only with her draw (i), excluding the off-diagonal combinations and imposing an artificial dependence between partners.  That makes the diagonal-to-product move a **specification fix**, while the 900 vs 1,600 vs 10,000 decision is a separate simulation-accuracy question. 

Because couples are a majority of the pooled household-years, this is not a minor robustness point. The note records roughly 7,438 couples out of 12,445 pooled household-years, so a misrepresented couples feasible set is first-order for your opportunity-vs-preference decomposition. 

## My decision

Do **not** rebuild the couples data immediately. First, do three things in order:

```text
