This keeps the current estimation track clean while preparing the next, better specification. It also prevents you from starting a huge data rebuild before confirming the exact construction code and computational implications.

## Why not rebuild immediately?

The product correction is upstream of almost everything. The note says this change is fixed at data preparation, before EUROMOD and before the GSUR merge. Moving from diagonal to product means rebuilding couples data, rerunning EUROMOD on new joint alternatives, re-merging GSURv2, re-stacking P3a, and then re-estimating. 

That is a large data-build cycle. It is worth doing, but it should be authorized as a new cycle, not inserted midstream into the current SA2-readiness process.

