## Why combine the couples-product and wage-occupation issues?

Because the future rebuild should define a job draw as a coherent package:

```text
partner job = hours × occupation × wage × GSUR/opportunity variables × disposable income
```

If you fix couples by moving from diagonal pairing to a product sample, but keep wages drawn independently of occupation, then the joint feasible set becomes larger but may still contain incoherent job packages.

If you condition wages on occupation but keep couples as the diagonal (i=i), then each partner’s marginal job package improves, but the joint couple feasible set remains wrong.

The natural next-cycle target is therefore:

```text
couples product-sample choice sets
+
occupation-conditional wage offer structure
```

with the size chosen under one computational budget.

